# Immutable publisher captures.
#
# `data/source/*/raw/` holds bytes exactly as a publisher served them, pinned by
# SHA-256 in that domain's artifact lock. The whitespace inside them is the
# publisher's, not this repository's: state legislature sites indent their
# markup with tabs and leave trailing spaces on thousands of lines, and an
# independent audit's `git diff --check` failed on precisely that.
#
# There is no correct fix on the repository's side. Stripping the whitespace
# would change bytes the lock pins and break every rights determination and
# transcription resting on them, and re-acquiring would not help because the
# publisher would serve the same thing again. So whitespace checking is turned
# off for captured bytes and stays on everywhere else — authored source, docs
# and generated JSON are all still checked, which is the point of the check.
data/source/*/raw/** -whitespace
